" http://localhost:24688/v1/chat/completions \ -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ -d '{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Reply with exactly: chat-ok"}],"max_tokens":16}' HTTP 200 content: chat-ok usage: 20 total tokens /v1/messages -> HTTP 200 content: messages-ok /v1/responses -> HTTP 200 output: responses-ok /v1/embeddings -> HTTP 200 1024-dim embedding ``` The after leg ran in a worktree that additionally carried the pending dashboard `schema.d.ts` regeneration, which is types-only and cannot change proxy behavior QA observations: - /v1/messages never leaked; 200 on both legs - Titan reports the leak as three schema violations - Live batch execution itself is exercised in #36634 ## Type 🐛 Bug Fix ## Caveats (if any) - `bedrock_tags` and `s3_output_bucket_name` registered but untested live - Only the five documented Bedrock batch fields are covered ### Final Attestation - [x] The tests check the right things, including the edge cases, and regressions in the respective real-world customer use-cases are not possible after this PR <!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY --> --- > [!NOTE] > <sup>[Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) is generating a summary for commit 3312f0beeac1e47c2093367edc06e5ef981bce41. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup> <!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->

